# HKU VPN configuration
# Copy this file to ~/.vpn/hku.env and fill in your details.

# Your HKU email (uid@connect.hku.hk for students, uid@hku.hk for staff)
HKU_USER=youruid@connect.hku.hk

# All locations use HKU's official VPN server, vpn2fa.hku.hk.
# Existing HKU_ENDPOINT=hk settings remain accepted for compatibility.

# Optional: override host-side proxy ports if 1080/1088 are already in use
# (e.g. you have Surge, Clash, or another local proxy on these ports).
# The container always exposes ports 1080/1088 internally; these settings
# only change what your Mac sees.
# HKU_SOCKS_PORT=11080
# HKU_HTTP_PORT=11088

# Advanced: pin the public entry point and both redirect backends to real
# addresses for the whole session. This also avoids fake-IP DNS inside Docker.
# Do not use a fake-IP address (for example, Surge Enhanced Mode's 198.18.0.0/15).
# The addresses below are RFC 5737 documentation addresses; replace every one
# with a current real-DNS result before enabling this option.
# HKU_RESOLVE=vpn2fa.hku.hk:192.0.2.10,vpn2fa-a.hku.hk:192.0.2.11,vpn2fa-b.hku.hk:192.0.2.12
